{"paper": "SSC-GD-05-Feb-2025-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 20, "tagged_count": 20, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "The average weight of Mandar, Ketan and Tushar is 45 kg. If the average weight of Mandar and Ketan be 43 kg and that of Ketan and Tushar be 48 kg, then the weight of Ketan (in kg) is:", "options": [{"text": "62", "added": false}, {"text": "47", "added": false}, {"text": "67", "added": false}, {"text": "57", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "47"}, {"n": 2, "text": "A work can be finished in a day by 20 men, or by 30 women, or by 50 boys. 2 men and 5 boys work on alternate days and 6 women work on all days. If men work on the first day, the work is finished in ____ days.", "options": [{"text": "3.3", "added": true}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": true}, {"text": "2.7", "added": true}], "options_source": "added", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "alternate-days", "key_answer": "3 1/3"}, {"n": 3, "text": "The selling price of a fan is ₹7,392. If profit percentage is 32%, then what is the cost price (in ₹) of the fan?", "options": [{"text": "5,200", "added": false}, {"text": "5,400", "added": false}, {"text": "5,600", "added": false}, {"text": "4,800", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "5,600"}, {"n": 4, "text": "If 2% of x = 348, then x is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "17400", "added": false}, {"text": "34900", "added": false}, {"text": "17500", "added": false}, {"text": "34800", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "17400"}, {"n": 5, "text": "LCM and HCF of two numbers are 168 and 14 respectively. If one of the numbers is 42, then find the other number.", "options": [{"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "58", "added": false}, {"text": "57", "added": false}, {"text": "56", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "application-problems", "key_answer": "56"}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": "4(3−√2)"}, {"n": 7, "text": "The simple interest on a principal amount (in ₹) is ₹824 for a period of 4 years at the rate of 8% per annum. The principal amount (in ₹) is:", "options": [{"text": "2577", "added": false}, {"text": "2573", "added": false}, {"text": "2571", "added": false}, {"text": "2575", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "rate-time-principal", "key_answer": "2575"}, {"n": 8, "text": "What will be the difference between the sale price (in ₹) of a book with a marked price ₹1,500 under the following discount schemes? (i) Two successive discounts of 20% each (ii) Two successive discounts of 30% and 10%", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": "15"}, {"n": 9, "text": "Shan has ₹1612 with him. He divided it amongst his sons Piyush and Manoj and asked them to invest it at 8% rate of interest compounded annually. It was seen that Piyush and Manoj got same amount after 12 and 13 years respectively. How much (in ₹) did Shan give to Piyush?", "options": [{"text": "687", "added": false}, {"text": "875", "added": false}, {"text": "837", "added": false}, {"text": "775", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-instalments", "key_answer": "837"}, {"n": 10, "text": "The smallest natural number which is divisible by 26, 8, 11 and 13 is:", "options": [{"text": "1201", "added": false}, {"text": "1082", "added": false}, {"text": "1126", "added": false}, {"text": "1144", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": "1144"}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "early-late", "key_answer": "9"}, {"n": 12, "text": "Find the value of", "options": [{"text": "357", "added": false}, {"text": "342", "added": false}, {"text": "355", "added": false}, {"text": "360", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "360"}, {"n": 13, "text": "Evaluate: (-9) - (-60) ÷ (-15) + (-3) × 7", "options": [{"text": "-34", "added": false}, {"text": "-33", "added": false}, {"text": "-37", "added": false}, {"text": "-36", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "-34"}, {"n": 14, "text": "Sachin sold 152 chairs and had a gain equal to the selling price of 52 chairs. What is his profit percentage?", "options": [{"text": "47%", "added": false}, {"text": "62%", "added": false}, {"text": "52%", "added": false}, {"text": "57%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": "52%"}, {"n": 15, "text": "A university has 500 faculty members (male and female only) out of which females are 60%. The average height of females is 162 cm and that of males is 168 cm. What is the average faculty height (in cm) of the university?", "options": [{"text": "125.4", "added": false}, {"text": "176.4", "added": false}, {"text": "146.4", "added": false}, {"text": "164.4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "weighted-average", "key_answer": "164.4"}, {"n": 16, "text": "The mean proportional between 2.8 and 0.7 is:", "options": [{"text": "1.4", "added": false}, {"text": "1.8", "added": false}, {"text": "1.9", "added": false}, {"text": "1.2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": "1.4"}, {"n": 17, "text": "When difference between compound and simple interest for three years is ₹244 at 5% interest per annum, the principal is ₹______", "options": [{"text": "31425", "added": false}, {"text": "33200", "added": false}, {"text": "32000", "added": false}, {"text": "32420", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "si-ci-difference", "key_answer": "32000"}, {"n": 18, "text": "The price of fuel decreases by 55%, 10% and 20% in three successive months, but increases by 65% in the fourth month. What is the percentage increase/decrease in the price of fuel in the fourth month as compared to its original price?", "options": [{"text": "Increases by 51.62%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increases by 48.43%", "added": false}, {"text": "Decreases by 46.54%", "added": false}, {"text": "Decreases by 50.53%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": "Decreases by 46.54%"}, {"n": 19, "text": "If the edge of a cube is tripled, then its volume increases to _______ times its original volume.", "options": [{"text": "64", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": "27"}, {"n": 20, "text": "A man goes to Ahmedabad from Kolkata at a speed of 78km/hr and returns to Kolkata at speed of 91km/hr, through same route. What is his average speed (in km/hr) of the entire journey?", "options": [{"text": "78", "added": false}, {"text": "81", "added": false}, {"text": "84", "added": false}, {"text": "85", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": "84"}]}